Module Description
1. Process Management Module
This module manages the processes involved in the simulation. It allows users to enter process details and helps track the current state of each process.
2. Resource Allocation Module
This module manages the resources required by different processes. It keeps track of available resources, allocated resources, and the resources still needed by each process.
3. Deadlock Detection Module
This module checks whether a deadlock condition exists in the system. It analyzes the allocation of resources and identifies processes that may be waiting indefinitely.
4. Deadlock Avoidance Module
This module checks whether resource allocation can lead to an unsafe state. If the project implements Banker's Algorithm, this module uses it to check whether the system is in a safe state before allowing resource allocation.
5. Banker's Algorithm Module
This module calculates the remaining resource requirements and checks for a safe sequence of processes. It helps determine whether the system can complete all processes without entering a deadlock.
6. Simulation Module
This module runs the deadlock simulation based on the input provided by the user. It displays process execution, resource allocation, and the final system status.
7. User Interface Module
This module provides an interface for users to enter process and resource information and view the simulation results in an understandable format
